Article 3 (Orders to Leave the Courtroom, etc.)
The presiding judge may restrain or order the removal of any of the following persons from the courtroom: <Amended on December 29, 2006.>
1. A person engaging in audio recording, video recording, photography, live broadcasting or similar activities (hereinafter referred to as "recording or filming activities") without the presiding judge's permission;
2. A person eating food or smoking;
3. A person interfering with proceedings by speaking loudly or causing a disturbance in the courtroom.
